    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d748">

                <pb facs="1064" n="1044" sameAs="frus:frus1950v07/pg1044"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">795.00/11–550: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Korea</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Drumright</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Seoul</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-11-05T18:00:00+09:00">November 5, 1950—6
                            p. m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received November 5—8:05 a. m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>337. ReEmbtel 332<anchor n="1" xml:id="d748-f1"/> on Chinese Communist activity
                    in North Korea. According Eighth Army Intelligence, only significant development
                        <pb facs="1065" n="1045" xml:id="pg1045"/> emerging past two days has been
                    spotting of considerable southbound vehicular traffic at various Yalu River
                    crossings in northwest Korea. Inasmuch as Chinese originally entered North Korea
                    with only three days’ rations and 100 rounds ammunition each, it surmised
                    southward traffic largely of supply character. With UN forces in Eighth Army
                    area regrouping and generally on defensive, few prisoners have been taken past
                    two days and only one found to be of Chinese race. No hostile air activity
                    reported past two days which perhaps due bad weather.</p>
                <p>Reports from Tenth Corps area which delayed as much as 30 hours in receipt here
                    indicate US Marines in contact with Sino-Communist unit about 20 miles north
                    Hamhung.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Drumright</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
